Acceptance Criteria
Identification of HK ETF Trades

Given a trade is captured in the system,
When the trade has stock.exchange = 104 And sub asset type = 118,
Then the system should classify it as an HK ETF trade for fee determination purposes. Stamp Duty Fee Exception

Given a trade is identified as an HK ETF trade (stock.exchange = 104 and sub asset type = 118),
When fees are calculated for the trade, Then stamp duty fee must not be applied and the stamp duty fee amount must be 0.
No Impact on Other Trades

Given a trade does not meet both conditions (stock.exchange = 104 and sub asset type = 118),
When fees are calculated, Then stamp duty fees should be charged as per existing rules with no change in current behaviour.

2.Identification of LSE IE trades

Given a trade is captured in the system,
When the trade has stock.exchange = 361
And company domicile = IE,
Then the system should classify it as an LSE IE trade for fee determination purposes.
Stamp Duty Fee Exception

Given a trade is identified as an LSE IE trade (stock.exchange = 361 and company domicile = IE),
When fees are calculated for the trade, Then stamp duty fee must not be applied
And the stamp duty fee amount must be 0. No Impact on Other Trades

Given a trade does not meet both conditions (stock.exchange = 361 and company domicile = IE),
When fees are calculated, then stamp duty fees should be charged as per existing rules with no change in current behaviour.